When a page asks for full screen in a window that’s already full
screen, Ladybird gives it full screen at once and hides its own UI.
And when the page leaves, the window goes back to the full screen the
user chose. Chromium does the same: FullscreenController::
EnterFullscreenModeForTab() records state_prior_to_tab_fullscreen_ as
STATE_BROWSER_FULLSCREEN, and enters tab full screen without changing
the window. And ExitFullscreenModeForTab() then returns to browser full
screen rather than to a normal window.
